---
description: Non-negotiable rules of the More than a Hack 2027 challenge (data access, labels, tuning, reproducibility)
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the start of every task. Answer the user in French.

Hard rules (one violation can disqualify the team; when in doubt, stop and ask):

1. NEVER read, print, cat, head, grep, open, plot or summarise frame-level content of `data/`,
   `cache/`, `*.mp4`, `*_atd.*`, `*_homography.csv`, `*_smart_tagging.xml` or
   `cache/viewer_pack.bin` -- not with tools, not in the terminal. You are a hosted LLM and the
   terms of use forbid giving it the match data or extracts. Only aggregate outputs (scores,
   counts, means, e.g. `python -m possession.diagnose`) may enter the conversation. To understand
   the match, ask the human to look in `tools/viewer.html`.
2. No human label of the provided match in any amount, and no rule or constant tied to specific
   frames of it. Labels come out of an algorithm.
3. Never tune or choose between versions using the public 5-minute ground truth
   (`evaluation/gt/*_public.csv`): it is for checking the pipeline only. Choose with the bench
   (`python -m validation.train ... --quick`, see AGENTS.md section 4).
4. No human-produced data about this match from any source (Opta, StatsBomb, ...).
5. Determinism: same inputs -> byte-identical `submissions/TercerHombre.csv`. No unseeded
   randomness, no network at inference, no pickles. Inference uses numpy + pandas only and must
   run on Python 3.9.
6. Never commit `data/`, `cache/`, `submissions/`, `validation/external_data/`, `.venv/`.
